# Useful Voice: more models (shared spec for all model workers)

Base branch: `feat/more-models`. It holds:
- `Tests/Fixtures/models/catalog.json`: THE model list (ids, names, providers, API model strings, badge, speed and accuracy 1-5, platforms, defaults). Each platform hard-codes its catalog and a test compares it to this file.
- `Tests/Fixtures/models/formatter-system-prompt.txt`: the exact AI formatter system prompt. Both platforms embed it verbatim; a test compares to the fixture.
- Parakeet contract stubs: `Sources/UsefulVoiceCore/LocalTranscription/ParakeetModels.swift` (macOS) and `windows/src/core/models/parakeet.ts` + `windows/src/main/parakeet.ts` (Windows). Keep the public signatures; the Parakeet workers implement them, the cloud/UI workers consume them.

Official API facts (verified 2026-10-18): `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-wasimjalali-Desktop-Personal-Project-useful-voice--claude-worktrees-voice-dictation-models-229d39/061b4f65-84ea-4896-beef-068a2317e034/scratchpad/model-api-spec.md`. Read it. Raw HTTP only (URLSession / fetch), no vendor SDKs (except FluidAudio and sherpa-onnx-node for Parakeet).

Owner's goals: dictation must stay rock solid; more model choice like Superwhisper; great speed and accuracy. The owner has Anthropic, Gemini, Deepgram keys and may get ElevenLabs credits.

## Product rules

1. Two choices, saved as catalog ids:
   - Voice model (transcription): one of the platform's `voice` entries. Default `deepgram:nova-3`.
   - AI formatting (language model): none (default, "Off") or one `language` entry.
   Migrate the existing engine setting: macOS `transcriptionEngine` deepgram -> `deepgram:nova-3`, whisperLocal -> `whisper:<active model id>`; Windows has only Deepgram -> `deepgram:nova-3`. First run keeps its current engine step; its choice writes the new setting.
2. Voice providers:
   - Deepgram: existing provider, `model` from the catalog's apiModel. Nova-3 Medical is English only: with an English or Auto pin send `language=en` (never detect_language across other languages); with any other pinned language fail fast with "Nova-3 Medical only speaks English. Pick another voice model or switch the language to English." Keyterms work as for Nova-3.
   - ElevenLabs Scribe v2: POST multipart to /v1/speech-to-text, `model_id=scribe_v2`, `file`=the WAV, `language_code` from the pin (omit for Auto), `tag_audio_events=false`, dictionary terms as repeated `keyterms` fields (at most 50, each under 50 chars and at most 5 words; skip others). Text from `text`, detected language from `language_code`. Map 401/403 -> key problem, 429 -> rate limited (retry like Deepgram), 5xx -> retry, deadline like Deepgram's size-based deadline.
   - Parakeet: through the contract (v2 English only: a non-English pin fails fast with a clear message; v3: the 25 European languages, else same kind of message).
   - Whisper local (macOS only): unchanged.
   - Never fall back silently between providers. A cloud model without its key: actionable error "Add your <Provider> key in Settings." A local model not downloaded: the existing "Download it in Settings" style.
3. AI formatting (off by default). When on:
   - Runs after transcription and BEFORE the Language Memory / dictionary / replacements / snippets step, so the user's own rules win. Skipped in raw mode, for an empty transcript, and for transcripts of 2 words or fewer.
   - Request: system = the fixture prompt verbatim. User message = `<vocabulary>a, b, c</vocabulary>\n<dictation>\n{text}\n</dictation>` (vocabulary line only when the dictionary has words; at most 100 words).
   - Gemini: POST v1beta/models/{apiModel}:generateContent, header x-goog-api-key, `systemInstruction`, `contents`, `generationConfig.thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel` = "low" for gemini-3.8-flash, "minimal" for gemini-3.6-flash and gemini-3.5-flash-lite; no temperature. Text = joined non-thought parts of candidates[0].
   - Anthropic: POST /v1/messages, x-api-key, anthropic-version 2023-06-01, max_tokens = clamp(input UTF-16 length, 256, 4096). claude-haiku-4-5 and claude-sonnet-4-6: temperature 0, no thinking field. claude-haiku-5-5: `thinking: {"type":"disabled"}`, no temperature. If a 400 body mentions "thinking", retry once without the thinking field. Text = joined `type:"text"` blocks.
   - Deadline 6 s (claude-sonnet-4-6: 10 s), and the dictation's cancel cancels it.
   - Guard (pure function, tested): trim; strip one wrapping code fence and one wrapping <dictation>...</dictation>; reject when empty, when output > 2x input length + 40 chars, when input >= 20 chars and output < 0.4x input length, or when output starts with an assistant preamble ("Here is", "Here's", "Sure", "Certainly", "I've", "I have", "Of course").
   - Any error, timeout, missing key or guard reject: deliver the unformatted transcript. Never block or lose the dictation. Log a Diagnostics line with the reason only (never the key or the text). The history record keeps the raw transcript as it does today; mark it formatted when the AI changed the text.
4. Keys: Deepgram (existing), ElevenLabs, Gemini, Anthropic. macOS: Keychain generic passwords under the existing service, accounts `elevenlabs-key`, `gemini-key`, `anthropic-key`, read once off the main thread and cached exactly like DeepgramKeyStore (generalise it; keep DeepgramKeyStore.shared working). Windows: stored encrypted with safeStorage exactly like the Deepgram key; the renderer only learns presence. Each key row has Save, Remove, Test (a cheap authenticated call: Gemini GET v1beta/models/{a catalog model}, Anthropic GET /v1/models, ElevenLabs GET /v1/models) and "Get a key" (https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys, https://aistudio.google.com/apikey, https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys). Never log keys; redact them from error text.
5. UI: the Settings "Engine" group becomes "Models" (anchor id `models`; keep `engine` working as an alias for anchors/deep links):
   - "Voice model" list and "AI formatting" list (the latter starts with an "Off" row). Shared column header row: Speed, Accuracy, then the right column.
   - Row: whole row selects (radio semantics, keyboard reachable, selected state visible and announced), a small monochrome monogram tile per provider (Deepgram "D", ElevenLabs "11", NVIDIA "N", Whisper "W", Gemini "G", Anthropic "A"; no vendor logos), the name, an optional badge chip (EN, NEW), two 5-segment meters (filled = rating), right column: "Cloud" for cloud models, or size + Download / progress / Delete for local ones. A cloud model whose key is missing shows "Add key" (moves to and focuses that key row) and can't be selected until the key is saved. A local model not downloaded starts the download when selected and becomes the voice model when ready.
   - "API keys" group below with the four key rows (the existing Deepgram row moves here).
   - Monochrome Useful brand (follow the existing tokens and components), light and dark, about 400 px narrow widths wrap cleanly. House voice: no em dashes, sentence case, contractions, no Oxford comma; no helper text under rows unless it prevents a real mistake.
6. Tests: E2E/behaviour level where possible (the repo's controller tests on macOS, dictationService + e2e Playwright on Windows), written failure-cases first. Real network calls are not available (no keys in CI): test request building and response parsing against recorded-shape fixtures, and providers against a local fake HTTP server where the repo already does that.
7. Docs: update AGENTS.md/README only where they describe engines, models or keys.
# Model API spec (researched 2026-10-18, official docs only)

## 1. Google Gemini API (generateContent, v1beta)

Docs read: ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models, /docs/deprecations, /docs/generate-content/thinking, /docs/generate-content/audio, /docs/models/gemini-3.8-flash, /api/generate-content, /docs/interactions.

- Endpoint: `POST https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/{model}:generateContent`
- Auth: `x-goog-api-key: <key>` header (docs' REST samples use it; the API ref also shows `?key=`). Prefer the header.
- Status: docs call generateContent "legacy" but "remains fully supported", no sunset date. New features land on `/v1beta/interactions`. generateContent still takes 3.8 Flash in the docs' own samples. Not confirmed: whether future models will be generateContent-compatible.

Current Flash-family IDs:
| ID | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `gemini-3.8-flash` | Stable, released 2026-09-02 | newest Flash; default thinking medium; `minimal` rejected with error |
| `gemini-3.7-flash` | Deprecated 2026-10-08 | requests are auto-routed to 3.8 Flash (response modelVersion says 3.8). Do not offer it |
| `gemini-3.6-flash` | Stable, 2026-07-21 | thinking levels minimal/low/medium(default)/high |
| `gemini-3.5-flash-lite` | Stable, 2026-07-21 | fastest; default thinking minimal; levels minimal/low/medium/high |
| `gemini-3.5-flash` | routes to 3.6 Flash, hidden | do not offer |
| `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` | Stable, shutdown 2027-05-07 | replaced by 3.5 Flash-Lite |
| `gemini-3-flash-preview` | Preview | replacement 3.6 Flash |
| `gemini-2.5-flash`, `gemini-2.5-flash-lite` | Stable | access limited to past users |

Text-only request with system instruction:
```json
{
  "systemInstruction": {"parts": [{"text": "..."}]},
  "contents": [{"role": "user", "parts": [{"text": "..."}]}],
  "generationConfig": {"temperature": 0.2, "maxOutputTokens": 1024,
                       "thinkingConfig": {"thinkingLevel": "minimal"}}
}
```
Response text: `candidates[0].content.parts[].text`, skipping parts with `thought: true`. Join the text parts. Blocked prompts return `promptFeedback.blockReason` and no candidates. `usageMetadata.thoughtsTokenCount` counts thinking tokens.

Thinking (3.x uses `thinkingLevel`, NOT `thinkingBudget`; `thinkingBudget` is for 2.5 only, and sending both gives 400):
- 3.8 Flash: low, medium (default), high. `minimal` returns an error. So lowest is `low`.
- 3.6 Flash: minimal, low, medium (default), high.
- 3.5 / 3.1 Flash-Lite: minimal (default), low, medium, high.
- Thinking cannot be fully turned off on 3.x Flash/Flash-Lite. Docs: `minimal` "does not guarantee that thinking is off". `thinkingBudget: 0` only works on 2.5 Flash / Flash-Lite.
- Casing: camelCase in REST (`thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel`). The interactions API uses snake_case `generation_config.thinking_level`.

Temperature: `generationConfig.temperature` is accepted. Not confirmed: Google's recommended value for Gemini 3 (I believe the docs say keep 1.0 for 3.x, but I did not read that this session). Test low values before relying on them.

Inline audio for transcription:
- Part shape: `{"inlineData": {"mimeType": "audio/wav", "data": "<base64>"}}` (proto-JSON; the API ref documents camelCase `inlineData`/`mimeType`, snake_case `inline_data` is also accepted by proto3 JSON but not confirmed in the docs I read). Put the text prompt in another part ("Generate a transcript of the speech.").
- Supported MIME: audio/wav, mp3, aiff, aac, ogg, flac, mpeg, m4a, l16, opus, alaw, mulaw, webm.
- Limit: 20 MB total request including prompt and system instruction (else use the Files API). Up to 9.5 h audio per prompt. 32 tokens per second of audio.
- Not confirmed: the audio page has no REST inline example (REST samples use the Files API `file_data`).

## 2. Anthropic Messages API (raw HTTP)

Docs read: platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/models/overview (docs.claude.com redirects here), /api/messages, /models/{haiku-4-5,haiku-5-5,sonnet-4-6,sonnet-5,sonnet-5-5}/overview, /build-with-claude/thinking-troubleshooting, /extended-thinking.

- `POST https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages`
- Headers: `x-api-key: <key>`, `anthropic-version: 2023-06-01`, `content-type: application/json`.
- Body: `{"model","max_tokens"(required),"system":"string or text blocks","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"..."}]}`. Response: `content` is an array of blocks; take `type=="text"` blocks and join `.text`. Do not assume `content[0]`.

Model IDs (Claude API):
| Model | ID | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Haiku 4.5 | `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` (alias `claude-haiku-4-5`) | legacy, retirement "not sooner than 2026-10-15", i.e. could go any time now |
| Haiku 5.5 | `claude-haiku-5-5` | latest, released 2026-10-07, $0.10/$0.50 per MTok (higher above 100k prompt) |
| Sonnet 4.6 | `claude-sonnet-4-6` | legacy, retirement not before 2027-02-17 |
| Sonnet 5 | `claude-sonnet-5` | legacy, not before 2027-06-30 |
| Sonnet 5.5 | `claude-sonnet-5-5` | latest, released 2026-09-28, $2/$10 |
Dateless IDs are pinned snapshots (4.6 onward).

Thinking defaults and how to turn it off (matters for latency):
- Haiku 4.5, Sonnet 4.6: off by default. Omit `thinking`.
- Sonnet 5: ON by default (adaptive). Send `"thinking": {"type": "disabled"}` (accepted).
- Haiku 5.5: ON by default. `{"type":"disabled"}` accepted only at effort `high` or below (400 with xhigh/max, and 400 if a per-message effort differs from the level in effect). Default effort is medium. Can also set `"output_config": {"effort": "low"}`.
- Sonnet 5.5: ON by default. `disabled` returns 400. Use `"thinking": {"type": "between_tools"}` (effort high or below) to skip up-front thinking.
- Never send `type: "enabled"` to 5.x models (400).
- Sampling: Sonnet 5, Sonnet 5.5 return 400 for non-default `temperature`/`top_p`/`top_k`. Haiku 5.5 doc says omit all three. Only Haiku 4.5 and Sonnet 4.6 take `temperature`. Build the request so 5.x omit it.
- Thinking tokens count against `max_tokens`; with thinking left on, a small max_tokens can truncate. Set a generous value.

## 3. ElevenLabs Speech to Text (Scribe)

Docs read: elevenlabs.io/docs/api-reference/speech-to-text/convert, /docs/overview/models, /docs/capabilities/speech-to-text.

- `POST https://api.elevenlabs.io/v1/speech-to-text`, header `xi-api-key: <key>`, `multipart/form-data`. Regional hosts exist (`api.us.elevenlabs.io`, residency hosts). Query `enable_logging=false` is enterprise-only zero retention.
- Fields: `model_id` (required), `file` (min 100 ms), `language_code` (ISO-639-1/3; omit for auto-detect), `tag_audio_events` (bool), `keyterms` (repeat the field per term), `diarize`, `timestamps_granularity` (`word`|`character`|`none`), `file_format` (`pcm_s16le_16` for raw 16 kHz mono PCM, else `other`), `temperature`, `seed`, `no_verbatim` (scribe_v2 only).
- Model IDs: `scribe_v2` (batch, current), `scribe_v2_medical` (batch, clinical), `scribe_v2_realtime` (streaming, WebSocket, ~150 ms partials, not for this POST), `scribe_v1` (deprecated, replaced by v2). The API ref page does not list the enum; values come from the models page.
- Keyterms: batch up to 1,000 terms, each under 50 chars and at most 5 words, none containing `< > { } [ ] \`. Adds a 20% surcharge. Realtime: 50 terms x 20 chars.
- Limits: 3 GB (capabilities page) vs "under 5.0 GB" (API ref), conflict, use 3 GB. 10 h max duration. Formats: WAV, MP3, M4A, OGG, Opus, FLAC, WebM, AAC, AIFF and video containers.
- Response (single channel): `text`, `language_code`, `language_probability`, `words[]` (`text`,`type`=word|spacing|audio_event,`start`,`end`,`speaker_id`), optional `transcription_id`, `audio_duration_secs`. Multichannel returns `transcripts[]`. With `webhook=true` you get 202.
- Audio events show up as text like "(laughter)" when `tag_audio_events=true`; set false for dictation.

## 4. Deepgram Nova-3 Medical

Docs read: developers.deepgram.com/docs/models-languages-overview, /docs/keyterm; announcement deepgram.com/learn/introducing-nova-3-medical-speech-to-text-api (via search result summary).

- `POST https://api.deepgram.com/v1/listen?model=nova-3-medical`, `Authorization: Token <key>`.
- Languages: `multi` plus English variants `en`, `en-US`, `en-AU`, `en-CA`, `en-GB`, `en-IE`, `en-IN`, `en-NZ`. (`nova-3-pharma` is English-only too, same variants.)
- `keyterm`: works on Nova-3 models; the announcement says Nova-3 Medical takes custom terms (up to 100) in both streaming and pre-recorded. Repeat the param (`&keyterm=a&keyterm=b`), multi-word via `+` or `%20`, no commas or weights. Hard limit 500 tokens total per request. `keywords` is not supported on Nova-3.
- Not confirmed from the main docs page: the keyterm doc page does not name `nova-3-medical`. Support rests on the Deepgram blog. Check with one live call.

## 5. Parakeet on macOS via FluidAudio

Sources: github.com/FluidInference/FluidAudio (README, Package.swift, source at tag v0.17.7), docs Documentation/ASR/*.md, HF cards. Package.swift and source read directly.

- Latest release `v0.17.7` (2026-10-08). SwiftPM: `.package(url: "https://github.com/FluidInference/FluidAudio.git", from: "0.17.7")`, product `FluidAudio`. (README's `from: "0.12.4"` snippet is stale.) swift-tools-version 6.0, no package dependencies.
- Min platform: `.macOS(.v14)`, `.iOS(.v17)`. Some newer models (Redux, Phonon-2) need macOS 15.
- API at v0.17.7 (verified in source):
```swift
let models = try await AsrModels.downloadAndLoad(to: customDir /*URL?, default nil*/, version: .v3 /*or .v2*/, progressHandler: ...)
let asr = AsrManager(config: .default)
try await asr.loadModels(models)          // README quickstart also shows configure(models:); source has loadModels
var state = TdtDecoderState.make()
let result = try await asr.transcribe(samples /*[Float], 16 kHz mono*/, decoderState: &state)
result.text
```
  The README shows `transcribe(samples)` with no decoderState, but v0.17.7 source requires `decoderState: inout TdtDecoderState` on all `transcribe` overloads (AVAudioPCMBuffer, URL, [Float]). Treat README as stale; compile against the pinned tag. Min samples enforced (`ASRError.invalidAudioData` below `minimumRequiredSamples`); audio over ~15 s is chunked. Do not hand-decode WAV bytes; use `AudioConverter` or pass a URL.
- Also public: `AsrModels.download(to:force:version:encoderPrecision:progressHandler:)` returns the dir, `AsrModels.load(from:configuration:version:)`, `modelsExist(at:)`, `defaultCacheDirectory(for:)`.
- Cache: default `~/Library/Application Support/FluidAudio/Models/<repo>` (repo = `parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-coreml` or `-v2-coreml`). Custom directory: yes, `to:` on `download`/`downloadAndLoad`, or `load(from:)` for pre-staged files. Expected files: `Preprocessor.mlmodelc`, `Encoder.mlmodelc`, `Decoder.mlmodelc`, `JointDecision.mlmodelc`, `parakeet_vocab.json`.
- Sizes: v3 about 480 MB (docs). v2 size not stated in docs. HF repo root is 3.59 GB because it holds many variants; the app downloads only the needed files. Not confirmed: v2 download size.
- v3 languages: 25 European languages (HF card; bg, hr, cs, da, nl, en, et, fi, fr, de, el, hu, it, lv, lt, mt, pl, pt, ro, ru, sk, sl, es, sv, uk). README adds Japanese but that is a separate model. v2: English only.
- Licenses: FluidAudio Apache-2.0. CoreML HF repos `FluidInference/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2-coreml` and `-v3-coreml`: metadata `cc-by-4.0` (v3 card body also says Apache 2.0 for the conversion code). Original NVIDIA `nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2` / `-v3`: CC-BY-4.0. CC-BY needs attribution to NVIDIA in the app's licenses screen.

## 6. Parakeet on Windows via sherpa-onnx Node

Sources: npm registry (sherpa-onnx-node, sherpa-onnx-win-x64), github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx (release `asr-models`, `nodejs-addon-examples/test_asr_non_streaming_nemo_parakeet_tdt_v2.js`), k2-fsa.github.io/sherpa/onnx/pretrained_models/offline-transducer/nemo-transducer-models.html.

- `sherpa-onnx-node` latest 1.13.8 (2026-09-10), Apache-2.0, main `sherpa-onnx.js`. Prebuilt binaries ship as optionalDependencies, one per platform: `sherpa-onnx-win-x64` (23 MB unpacked), `-win-ia32`, `-darwin-arm64/x64`, `-linux-x64/arm64`. No compile needed. npm picks the matching one at install, so a Windows build must install on Windows or CI must force `--os=win32 --cpu=x64`. Electron: native `.node` + onnxruntime DLL must sit outside the asar (`asarUnpack`). Not confirmed: Electron-specific behavior (not documented by sherpa-onnx); test with the Electron self-test.
- JS API (from the official example, parakeet v2 int8):
```js
const sherpa_onnx = require('sherpa-onnx-node');
const recognizer = new sherpa_onnx.OfflineRecognizer({
  featConfig: {sampleRate: 16000, featureDim: 80},
  modelConfig: {
    transducer: {encoder: '<dir>/encoder.int8.onnx', decoder: '<dir>/decoder.int8.onnx', joiner: '<dir>/joiner.int8.onnx'},
    tokens: '<dir>/tokens.txt', numThreads: 2, provider: 'cpu', debug: 0, modelType: 'nemo_transducer'}
});
const stream = recognizer.createStream();
stream.acceptWaveform({sampleRate: 16000, samples: float32Array}); // Float32Array in [-1,1]
recognizer.decode(stream);
const text = recognizer.getResult(stream).text;
```
  `sherpa_onnx.readWave(path)` reads a WAV. Hotwords example exists (needs `decodingMethod: 'modified_beam_search'`, `modelingUnit: 'bpe'`, `bpeVocab`, `hotwordsScore`; passed in `createStream`), the standard model release ships no `bpe.vocab`.
- Downloads (release tag `asr-models`, `https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/releases/download/asr-models/<file>`):
  - `sherpa-onnx-nemo-parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2-int8.tar.bz2`: 482,468,385 bytes (about 460 MiB)
  - `sherpa-onnx-nemo-parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-int8.tar.bz2`: 487,170,055 bytes (about 465 MiB)
  - (a v2 fp16 archive also exists, 1.12 GB.)
  - Format: `.tar.bz2`, extracts to a folder of the same name. v3 contents: `encoder.int8.onnx` (622 MB), `decoder.int8.onnx` (12 MB), `joiner.int8.onnx` (6.1 MB), `tokens.txt`, `test_wavs/`. v2 uses the same file names. Needs bzip2 extraction on Windows (Node has no built-in; bundle a lib, or have the app download the pre-extracted files from the csukuangfj HF repo `csukuangfj/sherpa-onnx-nemo-parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3-int8`, which hosts the raw files; v2 equivalent not checked).
- v3 languages: same 25 European languages as above. v2: English.
- Licenses: sherpa-onnx Apache-2.0. Models derive from NVIDIA Parakeet, CC-BY-4.0 (attribution required). The sherpa HF repo shows no license field; inherit from NVIDIA.

## Flags (could not confirm)
- Gemini: recommended temperature for 3.x; snake_case `inline_data` acceptance on REST; any plan to stop serving new models on generateContent.
- Anthropic: nothing unconfirmed on IDs. Haiku 4.5 may retire any day (earliest 2026-10-15).
- ElevenLabs: max file size conflict (3 GB vs 5 GB); API ref does not enumerate model_id values.
- Deepgram: keyterm on nova-3-medical confirmed only via a blog post, the docs page does not name it.
- FluidAudio: v2 size; README is stale on `transcribe` signature and SwiftPM version.
- sherpa-onnx-node inside Electron packaging not documented upstream.

